-names>Y.</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Reduction of all-trans retinal to all-trans retinol in the outer segments of frog and mouse rod photoreceptors</article-title>.<source>Biophys. J.</source><volume>88</volume>:<fpage>2278</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>2287</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15626704</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="bib6"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cornwall</surname><given-names>M.C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Fain</surname><given-names>G.L.</given-names></name></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>Bleached pigment activates transduction in isolated rods of the salamander retina</article-title>.<source>J. Physiol.</source><volume>480</volume>:<fpage>261</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>279</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7532713</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="bib7"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cornwall</surname><given-names>M.C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Fein</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>MacNichol</surname><given-names>E.F.</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name></person-group><year>1983</year><article-title>Spatial localization of bleaching adaptation in isolated vertebrate rod photoreceptors</article-title>.<source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source><volume>80</volume>:<fpage>2785</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>2788</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6573679</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="bib8"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cornwall</surname><given-names>M.C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Fein</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>MacNichol</surname><given-names>E.F.</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name></person-group><year>1990</year><article-title>Cellular mechanisms that underlie bleaching and background adaptat