irsov</surname><given-names>M.L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Golobokova</surname><given-names>E.Y.</given-names></name><name><surname>Govardovskii</surname><given-names>V.I.</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Two-stage quenching of cone phototransduction cascade</article-title>.<source>Sensornye Sistemy.</source><volume>21</volume>:<fpage>55</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>59</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Golobokova</surname><given-names>E.Y.</given-names></name><name><surname>Govardovskii</surname><given-names>V.I.</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Late stages of visual pigment photolysis in situ: cones vs. rods</article-title>.<source>Vision Res.</source><volume>46</volume>:<fpage>2287</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>2297</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16473387</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Govardovskii</surname><given-names>V.I.</given-names></name><name><surname>Fyhrquist</surname><given-names>N.</given-names></name><name><surname>Reuter</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuzmin</surname><given-names>D.G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Donner</surname><given-names>K.</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>In search of the visual pigment template</article-title>.<source>Vis. Neurosci.</source><volume>17</volume>:<fpage>509</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>528</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11016572</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hamer</surname><given-names>R.D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Nicholas</surname><given-names>S.C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Tranchina</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name